        "body": "Hi @dadezzz.  Thanks for the more detailed steps; I've reproduced the issue.  👍\r\n\r\nI believe that #14243 may have amplified one inconsistent behaviour in how non-restricted users are treated for public repositories -- some of the previous code paths would not write their access table records, and some would.  The centralized behaviour was to *not* write their records, but this behaviour is not correct as it causes problems with the repo search (as you've found), as well as few other subtle application areas.\r\n\r\nProposed patch in #15099."
      },
